UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w9-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260903
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260904
SUMMARY:VERTICAL 60 min WITH INTERVALS - stairwell. Warm up 10 min steady
 \, then 3 x (5 min HARD up at 90-95% HRmax + 3 min EASY SkiErg or rower)
 . Walk down between reps. Steady climbing for whatever time is left. Thi
 s is the only hard session of your week and it does two jobs: uphill int
 ervals for Madeira (the research wants 15-20% of training hard\, nearly 
 all of it on incline) and compromised running for Hyrox. The erg station
 s are deliberate - upper-body and aerobic\, so they add nothing to the e
 ccentric load your quads are already carrying.
DESCRIPTION:Week 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g car
 b/h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags an
 d no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry
  400-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage
 \, not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thursday's vertica
 l becomes intervals - the plan had no hard sessions at all through weeks
  7-8\, which was a gap. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% hard
 \, with the hard work on incline.\n59 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
