DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pack\, 
 walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m of d
 escent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\, so
 reness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no travel
 .
DESCRIPTION:Week 9 of 17 - Build\nGUT TRAINING STARTS. Target 60-80 g car
 b/h by week 14\, from 40-50 now\, +10 g every two weeks. No drop bags an
 d no crew at Madeira - only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart - so you carry
  400-500 g of carbohydrate yourself. Rehearse the weight and the stowage
 \, not just the products. INTENSITY STARTS THIS WEEK. Thursday's vertica
 l becomes intervals - the plan had no hard sessions at all through weeks
  7-8\, which was a gap. Target distribution is 80-85% easy\, 15-20% hard
 \, with the hard work on incline.\n61 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w10-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min - the day after the long day. Zero i
 mpact. THIS IS THE FIRST THING TO CUT when work bites.
DESCRIPTION:Week 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail runners\, inj
 ury weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebounding 15-37%. 
 Yo-yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. This dip is
  planned and the rebound is controlled.\n56 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
